  "interpretations_not_measurements": [
    {
      "assessment": "The observed forced-some regression cannot be attributed to dynamic key-path construction or projection in this optimized binary: selection is a direct field test. This does not prove equal timing, because the surrounding generated code differs.",
      "id": "no_runtime_keypath_overhead_explanation"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "The additional source-array retain call is a plausible contributor to the roughly 2 ns increase in empty-unforced independent medians. Assembly alone does not establish causation or quantify the cost; it is not a new timing measurement.",
      "id": "plausible_empty_path_cost"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "The original forced-some-64 result remains unresolved by assembly. A bounded balanced repeat using the same binaries and longer samples is warranted; preserve the original campaign and include neighboring forced controls. Native macOS qualification is stronger evidence for the shipping target. Changing the key path to a closure is not justified by runtime-key-path overhead in this inspection.",
      "id": "focused_confirmation_warranted"
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Inspection is specific to these binary hashes, Swift 6.3.2, and x86_64 Linux. It does not establish Apple-platform code generation or timing.",
    "Static disassembly cannot prove or exclude a repeatable microarchitectural performance regression.",
    "The source-array retain is a concrete code difference, but its contribution to the observed empty-control timing is an inference.",
